{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "The only completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, PCA, single profile) yielded a weak 48.5% accuracy, giving us a single low baseline with no information about whether the image modality carries useful signal. The most critical uncertainty right now is whether image features contribute at all, since the entire premise of 'multimodal cellular profiling' depends on it. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest way to isolate the image modality's contribution: it matches config_001's singleprofile setting and uses a standard pretrained encoder (resnet50) analogous to PCA as a 'default' representation, so the comparison directly tests modality value without confounding fusion strategy, aggregation, or encoder complexity. If image-only accuracy substantially exceeds 48.5%, it justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal fusion; if it is comparable or worse, we should focus on improving RNA representations (scvi, scgpt) and profile settings. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most important design axis with 8 experiments still remaining."
}

